@pytest.fixture(scope="session")
def settings() -> Settings:
    """Settings for the suite: the real database, and everything else in-process.

    The hashing cost is the one override that is about speed rather than
    isolation. Argon2 at the production parameters takes tens of milliseconds
    *by design*, and every test that needs a user pays it — which is exactly
    what ``HASHING_*`` exists for. The floor Keel enforces is still respected;
    this is the cheapest configuration it will accept, named rather than
    restated so raising the floor does not leave a stale literal here.
